SUMMARY:Mt. Mitchell to Winter Star\, 8.4mi\, 2\,900ft\, Fitness Hike
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Description:** Out and back diff
 icult\, rugged and challenging high mountain forreat hike with beautiful m
 ountain flora (picture) and fauna\, and many gorgous vistas. Trailhead beg
 ins on the Black Mountain Crest Trail ( at Mt. Mitchel) from the picnic ar
 ea (lower parking lot) to Winter Star Mountain. We will be hiking up and o
 ver peaks that are above 6\,000' (Mt. Mitchel's elevation is over 6\,400 f
 eet).. This hike includes some rugged rocky sections with steep rope assis
 t and ladder climbs. This hikes is specifically for conditioned hikers. Pl
 ease be sure of your hiking ability before signing on.\n\n**PACE:** All fi
 tness hikes have a brisk steady pace\, adjusting for trail conditions\, an
 d regrouping as needed. Due to steepness of grade and rugged conditions we
  will probably average about 2.5 mph.\nIf you sign up and change your mind
  even if on a waitlist\, change your RSVP to "not attending" to free up yo
 ur reservation.\n\n**Weather:** Cancelations due to wet or predicted storm
 y weather conditions will be announced on or before 7:00 am hike day. Temp
 eratures are usually 10+ degrees colder than Asheville and often windy.\n\
 n**CAR POOL:** Two options I will be at the Ingles Market on Weaver Blvd\,
  Weaverville by the Gas pumps leaving at 8:25 am\, or Asheville hikers can
  meet at the Folk Arts Center parking lot on the BRP at 8:25 am.. Please p
 ost where you plan to meet otherwise see you at the Mt. Mitchel picnic are
 a trailhead at 9:30.\n\nDriving to Mt. Mitchell picnic area: From Ashevill
 e\, take the Blue Ridge Parkway north/east past the various Craggies to Ro
 ute 128. Turn left toward Mt. Mitchell. Drive all the way to the Mt. Mitch
 ell parking lot. The picnic area is to your left just as you enter the par
 king lot on the lower level.\n\nDogs are welcome\, but have a leash handy 
 in case we run into other hikers or dogs.\n\nHIKE LEVELS This one is **lev
 el 9-10.**\n\nHike Level (1) Up to 600 feet of elevation gain. Level (2) 6
 00'- 900'\; Level (3) 900' - 1200'\; Level (4) 1200' - 1500'\; Level (5) 1
 \,500' - 1\,800'\; Level (6) 1\,800' - 2\,100'\; Level (7) 2\,100' - 2\,40
 0'\; Level (8) 2\,400' - 2700'\; Level **(9) 2700' - 3000'** Level (10) 30
 00' - 4000'\; ULTIMATE HIKES are hikes > 4\,000' elevation gain\; We post 
 3-4 of these hike challenges a year.\n\n**Release of Liability:**\nThe org
 anizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The funct
 ion of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or part
 icipate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agre
 e to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\,
  as a result of\, and associated with this event. In addition\, you acknow
 ledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.com/terms
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314890371
 /
